  "body": "## What changed\n\nA Circular whose source is the finished part (a whole model, `SrcRef::Entity` with `part_solid` true) is now judged against that part. `depth_law_of` (`crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`) gave every Circular `DepthLaw::None`, so a circle typed through the part's wall generated with no warning on the operation. It now takes `DepthLaw::Section` (the section and solid laws Contour, Face and the picked pockets answer to) through one shared function:\n\n```rust\npub(super) fn authored_law(src: &SrcRef) -> DepthLaw  // Entity -> Section; Stock, Selection -> None\n```\n\nIt is written for every kind that cuts geometry typed by hand (Circular's centre and radius here; the Slot's endpoints and width in #1537, where SKULL can call it; coordination comment on #1537). It runs after `depth_law_of`'s `part_solid` early return, so a Stock source (or an entity that is the setup's stock) still cuts unjudged. A picked Circular keeps its law (`None`).\n\n**Root cause / readings.** The old contract said \"the source is the material to remove, not a part to keep\", which holds only for a Stock source. On main, in the readings taken (radius-12 circle in a radius-10 through hole, 6 mm end mill, 0.5 left), the operation carried **0 warnings** (status ok, no MCP `verify` finding on the op). The post was held only by the program-level stock sim (`post blocked - gouge: program cuts below the model in 719 cell(s), worst 8.00 mm`). Now the operation itself carries blocking `Warning::Gouge`s on the moves that enter the wall (1028 over MCP), `held_by: [\"C1\"]`.\n\n## How tested (each pin mutation-checked)\n\nNew `crates/app/tests/circular_entity_law.rs`:\n- `a_whole_model_circle_typed_through_the_hole_wall_is_a_gouge_and_never_posts`: Entity source, gouge on the op, `posting::post_setup` refuses with \"post blocked\", no file written.\n- `a_whole_model_circle_inside_the_modeled_hole_stays_clean`: radius 10, no gouge, and the path equals the Stock source's move for move (judging never moves the tool).\n- `a_stock_source_still_cuts_the_typed_circle_unjudged`: the radius-12 circle on Stock carries no gouge.\n- `over_mcp_the_whole_model_circle_is_judged_the_same`: import_model / set_stock from_model / add_operation Circular on \"part\" / generate / verify: the op's own blocking gouge findings, `ok` false, `held_by` C1; the legal circle verifies `ok` true.\n\nNew in-crate `operation::authored_law_tests` (the law table): Entity -> Section, picked Circular -> None, Stock / stock entity (`part_solid` false) -> None, `authored_law` alone.\n\nMutations (each reverted after):\n- M1 Circular arm back to `DepthLaw::None`: the wall test, the MCP test and `a_whole_model_circular_is_judged_against_the_part` fail.\n- M2 `authored_law` judges picks (`Selection -> Section`): `a_picked_circular_keeps_its_law` and `the_shared_authored_law_reads_the_source_alone` fail.\n- M3 `part_solid` early return dropped and Stock judged: `a_stock_source_still_cuts_the_typed_circle_unjudged` and both table tests fail.\n- M4 `Entity -> Contain`: the table tests fail (the integration wall test also passes under Contain, which convicts the wall too; the decision file says why Section).\n\nQuick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green on 6162e8b1 (app suites 560 s, ui suites 47 s, 0 failed). Clippy: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No golden changes: no golden or existing test runs a Circular with an entity source (mill2d_b and units_in_refusals use Stock or picks, circular_pick uses picks).\n- Known conservative cost (decision file): under `Section` a typed true circle finished to size (stock to leave 0) in a coarse STL hole is convicted by the chord sagitta (32-chord radius-10 hole: refused; 128-chord: clean). Leaving 0.05 mm or a finer mesh clears it.\n- A picked Circular cut below its picked floor carries no warning on the op (the post gate's sim holds it): filed as #1550 (P3, effort:high).\n- MCP `generate`'s reply `status: \"ok\"` is freshness for every kind; findings ride `verify` (unchanged, cross-kind).\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/1543-circular-entity-law.md`.\n\nNot stacked: #1537's branch did not exist on the remotes when this started; the shared law lives here, and #1522 touches the neighbouring Slot arm of the same `match` (a one-line merge if both land).\n\nBranch cut from upstream/main 67329c86 (fork main synced at v0.19.0).\n\nChangelog: A Circular whose source is the finished part is judged against it: a circle typed through a wall carries a blocking gouge on the operation and never posts; a Stock source still cuts unjudged (#1543)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1543\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
